<title>POLAND: Polish 1996 trade gap up to $12.7 bln -statoffice.</title>
<headline>Polish 1996 trade gap up to $12.7 bln -statoffice.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's registered trade gap rose 106 percent to $12.7 billion in 1996 from $6.15 billion in 1995, the Central Statistical Office said (GUS).  </p>
<p> POLISH TRADE		   JAN-DEC 1996	 JAN-DEC 1995</p>
<p> Trade balance (in bln dollar)   12.697		   6.155</p>
<p> exports			    24.440		  22.895</p>
<p> imports			    37.137		  29.050</p>
<p> TRADE WITH EU		  JAN-DEC 1996	 JAN-DEC 1995</p>
<p> Trade balance		     7.542		   2.744</p>
<p> exports			    16.196		  16.036</p>
<p> imports			    23.738		  18.780 @</p>
<p>Note. GUS data is calculated on the basis of customs receipts and therefore substantially differs from data published by the National Bank of Poland, which uses cash flows to calculate the size of imports and exports.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
